        "payload": {
          "description": "About Contour\nContour Software has grown from a dozen people to over 2,000 staff across 3 cities, in less than 14 years.\nAs a subsidiary of Constellation Software Inc., we are proud to be part of a global enterprise software conglomerate that has grown to become one of the top 10 software companies in the world, with employees and customers in 100+ countries. With a broad-based and ever-growing portfolio of market-leading, vertical-market enterprise solutions covering more than 100 industry domains in predominantly mature markets, CSI's recipe creates the perfect environment for professionals to build fulfilling, long-term careers.\nWhat started as an R&D & Accounting back-office, has progressed into a full-service Global Centre serving all functions and departments, at the divisional as well as operating group/corporate level. Today Contour employees, located in Karachi, Lahore & Islamabad, are serving CSI divisions located in time zones spanning the globe, from Sydney to Vancouver. With the global growth of Constellation as the wind in our sails, we are only just getting started!\nThe Division\nJonas Premier Construction - a division of Constellation Software Inc. – is the market-leading cloud-based integrated construction management solution, for mid-sized General Contractors, Design Builders and Land Developers. Constellation companies are leading developers of technology solutions for vertical markets in North America, Europe and Australia. Jonas Software is the valued technology partner of over 8000 customers worldwide in 15 countries. Jonas is headquartered in Canada and also operates offices in the United States, the United Kingdom, and the Caribbean.\nThe Position\nWe are looking for Trainee Software Developers to join one of our R&D teams. The selected candidates will be trained for 3 to 3.5 months to become good developers capable of working on enterprise-level applications. After the end of the internship period, there is a good possibility of full-time employment based on satisfactory performance during the internship.\nThe chosen individuals will work out of the Contour Software Lahore resource center office, as an extension of the division-based R&D department.\nRequired Qualifications & Skills\nBS/MS in Computer Science or related field.\nStrong understanding of object-oriented programming principles.\nGood programming concepts and knowledge of .NET programming\nExposure to Generative AI, LLMs, RAG, Prompt Engineering, or AI-powered application development.\nStrong competencies in data structures, algorithms, and software design.\nStrong relational database concepts with SQL queries.\nGood level of knowledge of REST APIs.\nExperience and knowledge of Git.\nA quick learner, with attention to detail, and a commitment to meet deadlines.\nKnowledge of professional software engineering practices\nGood programming concepts and knowledge of frontend programming with JavaScript, AngularJS/Angular.\nGood communication skills in English.\nDisclaimer: At Contour, we attribute our success to the unique contributions of our diverse staff. We’re committed to fostering a culture of respect that thrives on the varied perspectives and experiences of all individuals we recruit, employ, promote, and compensate. Since day one, we’ve adhered to a policy that champions a work environment honoring the worth and dignity of each person while being free from all forms of employment discrimination.\nIn our continuous effort to promote inclusivity, we extend our commitment to individuals with special needs by providing reasonable accommodations. We actively encourage qualified individuals with special needs to apply for the various openings within our company. Should you require assistance in completing the application process or have any inquiries regarding special facilities, please do not hesitate to contact our HR team. Your unique talents and abilities are welcomed and valued here.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4484521392": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-03T23:29:51.290233+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "We are looking for a Full Stack Engineer to join our dynamic team.\nWe build scalable web applications using React/NodeJS/PostgreSQL. Our core technologies are Next.js and Supabase.\nThe ideal candidate has a strong foundation of backend logic & databases and has production experience.\nYou will be working directly with clients abroad on exciting cutting edge products.\nWho we are\nAZKY Tech Labs is a UK/Dubai based agency that specializes in building AI powered solutions (SaaS, Internal tools etc) for clients around the world. Over the past 5 years, we have worked with more than 100 foreign companies (startups, SMEs and Enterprises) in USA, UK, EU and Australia.\nWho You Are\nYou're a good fit if you have strong foundations and production experience in React/Node/PostgreSQL.\nAvailability : This role is for immediate hiring. It is not suitable for candidates who are currently employed full-time in another role.\nPrimary Interest : You have a strong, demonstrable passion for backend development. Your primary interest must be in server-side logic, APIs, and databases, not just UI development.\nTechnical Foundation : You must have solid experience with React.js, Node.js (ideally building REST APIs, e.g., with Express), Relational Databases (e.g., PostgreSQL or MySQL). You have architected databases from scratch.\nCore Concepts : You have a strong grasp of Data Structures, Algorithms, and Client-Server Architecture.\nKey Responsibilities\nDesign, develop, and maintain web and mobile applications\nWrite clean, maintainable, and efficient code following industry best practices.\nCollaborate with QA, and product teams to deliver robust features.\nOptimize application performance, scalability, and security.\nTroubleshoot, debug, and resolve technical issues across the stack.\nParticipate in code reviews, provide feedback, and ensure code quality.\nStay updated with emerging technologies and frameworks to enhance development efficiency.\nSoft skills\nGood English\nStrong attention to detail\nProactive, independent working style\nStrong communication and teamwork skills\nEffective time management and ability to prioritize tasks\nDesire to learn and grow as a developer\nSalary Range: Competitive\nPerks for you\nQuarterly Performance Bonus- based on performance and client outcomes\nCompany equipment (up to PKR 130k allowance to upgrade workstation)\nLaptop allowance (when you use your own laptop)\nInternet backup\nMedical insurance (dependents and parents included)\nDirect communication with clients and PMs (US, UK, EU) on a regular basis\nPaid time off\nFully remote and open work culture",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4485704382": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-03T23:29:51.290233+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "Dengage is a multinational SaaS company dedicated to delivering innovative solutions that drive digital engagement and enhance customer experiences. Our team is passionate about technology and committed to fostering an environment where talent can thrive and grow.\nWe are looking for a talented and motivated Full Stack Developer to join our engineering team and contribute to the development, enhancement, and maintenance of our SaaS platform.\nKey Responsibilities\nDesign, develop, and maintain scalable web applications using modern frontend and backend technologies.\nDevelop responsive, user-friendly interfaces using JavaScript, TypeScript, Vue.js, React, or similar frameworks.\nBuild and maintain backend applications, services, and RESTful APIs using C#, .NET Core, or similar technologies.\nDesign, develop, and optimize relational databases, including SQL Server or PostgreSQL.\nIntegrate frontend applications with backend services and third-party APIs.\nWrite clean, efficient, reusable, and maintainable code following software development best practices.\nTroubleshoot, debug, and resolve application performance and functionality issues.\nParticipate in code reviews, technical discussions, and system design activities.\nCollaborate with product managers, QA engineers, and other developers to deliver high-quality features.\nImplement appropriate security, authentication, and authorization mechanisms.\nWrite and maintain unit tests and integration tests.\nParticipate in Agile/Scrum development processes and contribute to continuous improvement.\nSupport application deployment, monitoring, and ongoing optimization.\nRequirements\nTechnical Skills\nBachelor's degree in Computer Science, Software Engineering, Information Technology, or a related field.\n3–5 years of professional experience in full stack software development.\nStrong understanding of object-oriented programming (OOP), data structures, and software development principles.\nHands-on experience with C#, ASP.NET Core, .NET Core, or similar backend frameworks.\nStrong proficiency in JavaScript, TypeScript, HTML5, and CSS3.\nPractical experience with Vue.js, React.js, or similar frontend frameworks.\nExperience developing and integrating RESTful APIs.\nGood understanding of relational databases, SQL queries, and database optimization.\nFamiliarity with Entity Framework Core or other ORM frameworks.\nExperience with Git and collaborative development workflows.\nUnderstanding of authentication, authorization, and web application security.\nFamiliarity with Agile software development methodologies.\nStrong debugging, analytical, and problem-solving skills.\nGood communication skills and ability to work effectively within a team.\nPreferred / Nice-to-Have Skills\nPrevious experience developing SaaS products or cloud-based applications.\nExperience with Microsoft Azure, AWS, or other cloud platforms.\nFamiliarity with Docker, containerization, and CI/CD pipelines.\nUnderstanding of microservices architecture and distributed systems.\nExperience with Redis, MongoDB, or other NoSQL databases.\nKnowledge of message queues such as RabbitMQ or Kafka.\nFamiliarity with automated testing frameworks.\nExperience working with high-volume data processing applications.\nExposure to marketing technology (MarTech), customer engagement platforms, or customer data platforms (CDP).\nBasic understanding of application performance monitoring and optimization.\nBenefits\nBenefits\nGrowth Opportunities: Access to professional development and career growth within a rapidly expanding SaaS company.\nCollaborative Culture: Work in a supportive and innovative environment where your contributions are valued.\nCompetitive Benefits: Enjoy a comprehensive benefits package.\nD.engage is an equal opportunity employer. We celebrate diversity and are committed to creating an inclusive environment for all Team Members.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4485917766": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-03T23:29:51.290233+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "About The Company\nEnergy Innovation: Policy and Technology LLC is a technology-focused organization based in Ketchikan, Alaska. The company designs and develops tools that support businesses across the technology sector, with products and services intended to address practical needs and help teams work effectively. Its Civic Innovation Lab brings together ideas, technology, and collaboration to explore solutions for business and community challenges.\nThe Ketchikan team works at a steady, sustainable pace and values time for careful, focused development. Team members are encouraged to communicate openly, learn from one another, and take ownership of their work. This environment is suited to people who are curious, adaptable, and interested in improving early ideas through thoughtful implementation and documentation.\nAbout The Role\nEnergy Innovation: Policy and Technology LLC is seeking a Junior Node.js Developer to contribute to the development and ongoing improvement of the Civic Innovation Lab’s technology platform. This is an opportunity for an early-career developer who is ready to build practical experience, learn from a mentor, and take responsibility for well-scoped work from initial discussion through implementation and review.\nYou will work with colleagues to understand business needs, help turn ideas into technical plans, and develop reliable software that supports users and internal teams. The role is collaborative and hands-on: you may contribute to prototypes, APIs, integrations, database improvements, and platform maintenance. Node.js is central to the position, while familiarity with Angular, Ruby on Rails, or infrastructure tools such as Ansible can help you work across the broader technology environment. The position offers an annual salary range of $68,000 to $99,000, depending on relevant experience and qualifications.\nQualifications\nApplicants should bring a foundation in software development and a genuine interest in building their skills with Node.js. Approximately one year of relevant experience, which may include internships, academic projects, or other practical development work, is preferred. You should be comfortable learning unfamiliar systems and applying feedback to improve your work.\nWe are looking for clear written and verbal communication, sound analytical thinking, and the ability to collaborate with people who have different areas of expertise. Strong candidates can break larger problems into manageable tasks, document decisions, and contribute constructively when requirements are still developing. Familiarity with JavaScript, API development, databases, authentication concepts, version control, or software testing is helpful. Experience with Angular, Ruby on Rails, or Ansible is beneficial but not required.\nResponsibilities\nCollaborate with business stakeholders and developers to clarify requirements and translate feedback into technical specifications, estimates, and actionable tasks. Contribute to prototypes that help the team assess ideas, communicate trade-offs, and identify opportunities for improvement.\nDevelop, test, document, and maintain Node.js services and application features. Support integrations with other parts of the platform, including systems built with Angular or Ruby on Rails, and help investigate issues that arise across service boundaries. Assist with implementing secure authentication and authorization flows, following established standards and seeking review when needed.\nHelp tune database queries and schemas to support reliable performance as workloads grow. Participate in code reviews, testing, release preparation, and service support, with appropriate guidance from experienced colleagues. Keep technical documentation useful and current, and raise risks, questions, and potential improvements early.\nBenefits\nThe role offers an annual salary of $68,000 to $99,000, commuter benefits, and a mentor matched to your professional interests and technology goals. You will have opportunities to develop practical skills, contribute to meaningful platform work, and learn in a team that protects time for focused development. Specific compensation and benefit details are subject to the company’s policies and the terms of employment.\nEqual Opportunity\nEnergy Innovation: Policy and Technology LLC is committed to providing a respectful and inclusive workplace. Employment decisions are based on role-related qualifications, skills, and business needs. All qualified applicants will receive consideration without regard to protected characteristics under applicable law. Candidates are encouraged to apply even if they do not meet every preferred qualification.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4485930641": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-03T23:29:51.290233+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "Uniti is a premier insurgent fiber provider dedicated to enabling mission-critical connectivity across the United States.\nWith a steadfast commitment to customer service, operational excellence, and superior network capabilities, Uniti builds, operates and delivers critical fiber-based communications services to connect and empower people and businesses.\n_________________________________________________________\nAbout The Role\nThe Software Developer II is responsible for designing, developing, supporting, and improving software solutions that help automate operational workflows and improve service delivery. This role works closely with engineering, operations, and business stakeholders to build reliable backend services, APIs, and automation tools in a collaborative remote environment. The ideal candidate brings strong Python and SQL skills, sound software engineering practices, and the ability to manage work effectively across Azure DevOps, GitHub repositories, and Microsoft Teams.\nWhat You'll Do\nDesign, build, test, deploy, and support software applications, APIs, and automation tools that improve team efficiency and service quality.\nDevelop backend services and integrations using Python and SQL in support of operational and business processes.\nCreate and maintain REST APIs and service integrations with internal systems, databases, and third-party/vendor platforms.\nWrite clean, maintainable, and secure code with attention to performance, reliability, logging, and error handling.\nAnalyze business and technical requirements, translate them into technical solutions, and support successful implementation.\nManage work items, user stories, and sprint-related activities in Azure DevOps (ADO), including story updates, task tracking, and status communication.\nUse Git and GitHub repositories for source control, branching, code review, pull requests, and release coordination.\nCollaborate with cross-functional teams through Microsoft Teams chats, channels, meetings, and other remote communication tools.\nEngage with stakeholders to gather requirements, provide updates, clarify priorities, and support solution adoption.\nSupport troubleshooting, root cause analysis, and issue resolution for production and non-production environments.\nParticipate in an on-call or after-hours support rotation as needed to support critical systems, deployments, or issue resolution.\nWork effectively in a remote environment while managing priorities, meeting deadlines, and maintaining strong communication with the team.\nDo You Have\nCollege degree and 3-5 years of related software development experience, or 7+ years of equivalent engineering/technical experience, or a combination of education and related experience.\nProfessional software development experience with a strong emphasis on backend development.\nStrong Python development experience in production or enterprise environments.\nStrong SQL skills, including writing complex queries, troubleshooting data issues, and working with relational databases.\nExperience developing or supporting REST APIs and system integrations.\nExperience with Git-based source control and collaborative development practices, including pull requests and code reviews.\nExperience working in Agile environments with Azure DevOps or similar work management tools.\nStrong analytical, problem-solving, and troubleshooting skills.\nStrong written and verbal communication skills and the ability to work effectively with technical and non-technical stakeholders.\nTechnical Skills - Python and Backend Development\nStrong proficiency in Python for application development, automation, data processing, and backend services.\nExperience building and supporting Python-based APIs or web services, preferably with FastAPI, Flask, or similar frameworks.\nUnderstanding of core Python concepts such as object-oriented programming, modular code structure, exception handling, and reusable component design.\nExperience working with API request/response patterns, JSON payloads, validation, authentication, and integration error handling.\nAbility to write asynchronous or concurrent Python code when needed for service integrations or long-running processes.\nExperience debugging Python applications, reviewing logs, identifying root causes, and resolving production issues.\nExperience writing secure and efficient database-driven code using Python and SQL.\nFamiliarity with testing and quality practices such as unit testing, integration testing, and code review.\nAbility to maintain readable, well-documented code and contribute to ongoing modernization and process improvement efforts.\nTechnical Environment\nProgramming / Scripting: Python, SQL\nBackend / API: REST APIs, FastAPI or similar Python web frameworks, service integrations, JSON-based interfaces\nDatabases: Oracle, MySQL, MariaDB, DB2, PL/SQL, relational database concepts\nTools / DevOps: Azure DevOps, Git, GitHub, CI/CD pipelines, Docker, Kubernetes/AKS\nCollaboration: Microsoft Teams, remote collaboration tools, stakeholder communication\nOperating Model: Agile delivery, backlog/story management, production support, after-hours support as needed\nEven Better\nExperience in telecommunications, network automation, service provisioning, or operational support environments.\nExperience with cloud platforms, containerized deployments, and CI/CD delivery practices.\nExperience supporting integrations with vendor or third-party systems.\nFrontend experience with JavaScript, TypeScript, React, or Next.js is a plus, but not required.\nPhysical Tasks- Standing Occasionally: 0-33% | Walking Occasionally: 0-33% |Sitting Continuously: 67-100% | Bending: Occasionally: 0-33% | Crouching: Occasionally: 0-33% | Pushing-Pulling: Occasionally: 0-33% | Carrying: Occasional: 0-33% | Reaching Above Head: Occasionally: 0-33% | Lifting-Lowering >1-15 lbs: Occasionally: 0-33% | Repetitive Hand Action: Medium Dexterity: Continuously: 67-100% | Fine Manipulating: frequently: 34% - 66%\nAudio Visual Needs - Hearing: Continuously: 67-100%| Near Vision: Continuously: 67-100% | Far Vision: Occasionally: 0-33% | Peripheral Vision: Occasionally: 0-33%\nEquipment Used in Job Performance: Computer, Printer, Telephone, Basic Office Supplies, Copier\nThe starting compensation range for this job is $67,100 to $88,000. Our compensation approach is designed to be fair and competitive. Pay for this role is based on factors such as your experience, skills, education, and location.\n_________________________________________________________\nActual base pay for this job will depend on the candidate's primary work location and other factors, such as relevant skills and experience.\nOur Benefits\nMedical, Dental, Vision Insurance Plans\n401K Plan\nHealth & Flexible Savings Account\nLife and AD&D, Spousal Life, Child Life Insurance Plans\nEducational Assistance Plan\nUniti is an equal opportunity employer. At Uniti, we celebrate the authenticity and uniqueness of our people and their ideas. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, genetic information, protected veteran status, current military status, disability, sexual orientation, marital status, creed, citizenship status, or any other status protected by law, and to give full consideration to qualified disabled individuals and protected veterans.\nNotice to Non-U.S. Citizens: Uniti, as a holder of licenses granted by the Federal Communications Commission, is required to notify and to obtain approval from federal regulatory agencies prior to granting certain system/network access to any non-U.S. citizen personnel. Offers of employment extended to non-U.S. citizens are contingent upon receiving the requisite approval from agencies overseeing compliance. Non-U.S. citizens are required to provide Uniti with the personal identifying information required to obtain the necessary approval prior to accessing certain systems and/or Uniti’s network. If you are not a U.S. citizen, please notify your recruiter or contact HR Legal as soon as possible for information on Uniti’s foreign personnel disclosure and approval requirements.\nNotice to Applicants: Depending on the position and its job functions, offers of employment may be contingent upon successful completion of certain pre-employment screenings, including but not limited to drug-screen, motor vehicle records check, or other pre-employment screening. All such screenings will be conducted by an external third-party with the Candidate’s written consent and in accordance with federal and state law. Refusal to authorize or submit to a required pre-employment screening may disqualify the candidate from employment. Any misrepresentation during the application or interview process may result in denial of employment, withdrawal of offer, or termination.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4485932432": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-03T23:29:51.290233+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "About The Company\nSynergisticIT is a technology-focused organization that helps connect aspiring and experienced professionals with opportunities in software development, data science, and related fields. The company supports candidates as they build in-demand technical skills and prepare for careers in the technology industry. Through practical learning, career guidance, and connections with employers, SynergisticIT works to help individuals pursue roles aligned with their abilities and professional goals. The company values continuous learning, adaptability, and a strong foundation in computer science and modern development practices.\nAbout The Role\nSynergisticIT is seeking a motivated Software Developer to contribute to the design, development, testing, and maintenance of software applications. This opportunity is suitable for candidates who are beginning or advancing their careers and are eager to apply their programming knowledge to real-world technical challenges. The successful candidate will work with development teams to understand requirements, create reliable solutions, and improve existing applications. Depending on project needs, assignments may involve web applications, backend services, databases, APIs, or cloud-based systems. Candidates should be prepared to learn new tools, accept constructive feedback, and grow their technical capabilities in a collaborative environment. Project placement and responsibilities may vary according to qualifications and client requirements.\nQualifications\nCandidates should have a bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Information Technology, Software Engineering, or a related field, or demonstrate equivalent practical knowledge. A solid understanding of programming fundamentals, object-oriented design, data structures, algorithms, and software development principles is expected. Familiarity with one or more languages, such as Java, Python, JavaScript, C#, or a comparable language, is desirable. Knowledge of SQL and relational databases is beneficial, as is exposure to HTML, CSS, web frameworks, REST APIs, version control systems such as Git, and software testing practices. Experience with cloud platforms, Agile methods, or CI/CD tools is an advantage but is not required for every assignment. Applicants should communicate clearly, approach problems analytically, and be willing to learn unfamiliar technologies. Relevant coursework, personal projects, internships, or professional experience may demonstrate applicable skills.\nResponsibilities\nDevelop, enhance, and maintain software features in line with functional requirements and technical specifications. Collaborate with developers, analysts, quality assurance professionals, and other stakeholders to clarify project needs and deliver dependable solutions. Write readable, maintainable, and well-documented code while following established standards and security practices. Participate in code reviews, testing, debugging, and issue resolution throughout the development lifecycle. Help identify opportunities to improve application performance, usability, reliability, and maintainability. Work with databases and APIs as required, and support integration between software components. Track assigned work, communicate progress and challenges, and contribute to team discussions and project documentation. Stay informed about relevant technologies and apply feedback to strengthen technical and professional skills.\nBenefits\nBenefits and employment terms may vary based on the specific position, project, work location, and employment arrangement. Depending on eligibility, offerings may include opportunities for technical training, career development resources, mentorship, and exposure to diverse projects and technologies. Eligible employees may also receive compensation and benefits in accordance with applicable company policies and local requirements. Details about compensation, benefits, work arrangements, and any project-specific conditions will be provided during the recruitment process. SynergisticIT encourages candidates to review the terms associated with each opportunity and discuss questions with the recruiting team.\nEqual Opportunity\nSynergisticIT is committed to fair and inclusive employment practices. Employment decisions are based on qualifications, skills, business needs, and applicable legal requirements. Candidates are considered without discrimination based on any status protected by applicable law. The company welcomes applicants from varied backgrounds and encourages individuals with relevant skills and a commitment to learning to apply.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4486054650": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-03T23:29:51.290233+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "Job Overview:\nJoin our team as a Software Engineer and be at the forefront of creating innovative software solutions. Collaborate with cross-functional teams to design, develop, and maintain cutting-edge applications that drive our technological success. If you're passionate about coding, problem-solving, and contributing to impactful software, we welcome you to apply.\nJob Responsibilities:\nDesign, develop, test, maintain and improve the software.\nManage individual project priorities, deadlines and deliverables.\nDevelop high-quality, scalable, and interactive web applications.\nQualifications:\nBS degree in Computer Science or Software Engineering.\n02 - 04 years of experience in software development in Microsoft based, one or more general-purpose programming languages.\nExperience working the following technologies: web application development, HTML, CSS, JavaScript/JQuery, Angular, CVW, PWA, ASP.NET, SQL, WCF, Web APIs, Version Controlling, Application Security and CI/CD.\nExperienced in using tools including: Visual Studio, SQL Server, Team Foundation Server.\nIT healthcare domain knowledge will be preferable.\nO/A levels background will be preferred.\nDetailed knowledge of the IIS/Web server.\nInterest and ability to learn other coding languages as needed.\nWorking proficiency and communication skills in verbal and written English.\nCompensation & Benefits:\n💰 Financial:\nCompetitive salary and bi-annual bonus.\nFast track and uncapped career growth for high performers.\nCompany-sponsored vehicle financing (car and bike).\nInterest-free loans.\nProvident Fund: CureMD matches up to 8% of your base salary.\n🏥 Health and Wellness:\nIn-house clinic with a team of certified male and female doctors with 24/7 telemedicine service.\nHospital treatment monitoring by company doctors.\nComprehensive health coverage for your immediate family (outpatient, inpatient, maternity and parents' inpatient).\nExclusive health benefits and discounts at top class clinics and labs.\n🤝🏻 Supportive Workplace:\nPick-up and drop-off services for female employees.\nIn-house daycare facility.\nIn-house gym and recreational area to unwind.\n📚 Continued Learning:\nCompany-sponsored trainings, workshops, development programs and retreats.\nPaid specialized trainings/certifications.\nThe Difference You’ll Make:\nAt CureMD, every role, whether senior or junior, plays a pivotal part in transforming healthcare. By joining our innovative team, you’ll contribute to groundbreaking technology that directly impacts patient care, enhances healthcare efficiency, and saves lives globally. Your skills and passion will drive meaningful change, helping us deliver solutions that support healthcare professionals in critical, real-time settings. Together, we’re not just advancing technology — we’re making a tangible difference in people’s lives. Together, let’s save lives.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4486161894": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-03T23:29:51.290233+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "At Zyte, we don't just collect web data—we solve complex web data challenges at scale. We are a globally distributed team that is bold, curious, and dedicated to building innovative ways to deliver clean, reliable web data from across the internet.\nData is our passion: We unlock access to open web data, empowering organizations—from startups to global enterprises—to power competitive intelligence, analytics, and AI pipelines\nRemote-first culture: Work from anywhere in the world. With over 260 Zytans across 33 countries, our strength comes from diverse backgrounds, perspectives, and skills\nEngineering excellence: We love diving deep into complex code bases, evaluating emerging technologies, and pushing technical boundaries. If you thrive on creative problem-solving and reliably delivering production-grade solutions, you will fit right in\nEstablished system design framework: We systematically analyze functional and product requirements alongside architectural trade-offs to make informed, sustainable design decisions\nReal-world distributed systems challenges: Tackle rare engineering problems in custom networking, high-throughput streaming, and large-scale orchestration under real-world operational constraints\nStrong product ownership: Work on a profitable, market-leading platform with dedicated time and resources allocated for architectural research and strategic feature engineering\nWhy This Role?\nZyte API fetches the web through a ladder of routes: plain HTTP, headless browsers, and, for the hardest targets, Edge—our own residential network of real devices. Edge is the tier that must succeed when everything else has failed. Today, a Rust peer on residential Windows PCs long-polls a single command-and-control service (CNC) over mTLS gRPC; CNC schedules fetches onto peers, runs a CONNECT proxy gateway, owns geo-routing, per-site cooldowns, and bandwidth quotas. It must grow from thousands of nodes to tens of millions of requests a day with rock-solid reliability.\nThe Edge Platform squad owns the control plane and data plane of this residential stack across Windows, Android, and Linux. The next step is building a proper Fleet Manager: a control plane with provider adapters (volunteer PCs, mobile-IP device farms, self-hosted nodes), a reconciler, rollout control, and metrics export sitting beside CNC as the data plane. You will design and operate that system—handling the scheduling, networking, proxying, and reliability work that turns residential devices into infrastructure other squads depend on. You will work directly with the Team Lead, a Principal Engineer, and partner engineering squads across Zyte.\nWhat You'll Do\nScale the data plane. Evolve CNC from a single-replica service into a horizontally scalable fetch scheduler: node selection that respects geo, site cooldowns, jail and per-peer quotas while avoiding detectable patterns, at 50-100M requests per day\nBuild the Fleet Manager control plane. Design and ship the inventory, health, configuration and software-rollout plane for the fleet: provider adapters, a reconciler, a rollout controller and an exporter to BigQuery, so a second device provider can be onboarded without bespoke scripts\nOwn the proxy path. Operate and improve the CONNECT proxy gateway and session handling on the edge, and work with the API squad on IP reputation, proxy leases and request scheduling so Edge slots cleanly into the platform's proxy plane\nEngineer the networking. mTLS gRPC between control plane and peers, long-poll and streaming semantics over unreliable residential links, NAT and carrier-grade NAT behaviour, and bandwidth accounting that is correct under contention\nMake it reliable. Define SLOs for availability, success and latency of the Edge route; build the metrics on peer count, drop-off and bandwidth that hold us and our supply partners accountable; run blue/green rollouts of CNC and peers safely\nShare production ownership. Take part in the squad's on-call rotation, lead incident post-mortems and turn operational lessons into platform improvements\nRaise the bar. Write RFDs for scheduling, fleet management and failover; review designs across the squad; and bring distributed-systems rigour (consistency, backpressure, idempotency, blast radius) to a young codebase\nRequirements\nWho You Are\n5+ years of production Rust experience, shipping and operating services you own end to end\nDistributed systems: you have designed and run schedulers, control planes or stateful services at scale, and can reason about consistency, partitions, backpressure and idempotency without a whiteboard\nDeep networking: TCP, TLS and HTTP at the handshake and packet level, gRPC and long-lived connections across NAT and lossy links, and what a client looks like on the wire\nProxy expertise: you have built or operated forward proxies, proxy gateways or residential/ISP proxy infrastructure, and understand IP reputation, session stickiness and pool health\nOps and reliability experience: SLOs and error budgets, observability you built yourself, production incidents you led, and comfort with being on call\nCross-platform awareness: comfortable with Rust running on Windows, Linux and Android targets, and with FFI boundaries when the data plane needs them\nAsync communication: strong written communication for a globally distributed, remote-first environment\nCurious problem solver: you like finding out why a system behaves the way it does under load, and fixing the cause rather than the symptom\nOur Tech Stack\nLanguages: Rust (tokio, tonic), C++ (Cronet) at the peer boundary; Python and Java in the services we integrate with\nProtocols: gRPC and protobuf over mTLS, HTTP CONNECT proxying, the Chromium network stack and our own browserless HTTP client\nInfrastructure: GCP and Kubernetes for the control plane, Terraform, blue/green deployments; multi-cloud (OCI, GCP) and data centres (Hetzner, Servers.com) across the wider platform\nData & Messaging: Valkey, BigQuery, Confluent Kafka\nMonitoring & Observability: Prometheus, Grafana, Loki, OpenTelemetry\nBonus Points\nMobile or desktop Rust: experience shipping Rust on Android, Windows or macOS, or binding Rust to C/C++ via FFI\nFleet or device management: reconcilers, rollout controllers, IoT or volunteer-computing fleets\nAnti-bot and fingerprinting: understanding of how TLS, HTTP and IP signals are used to classify traffic\nWeb scraping & crawling experience: familiarity with the technical challenges of large-scale web data extraction\nOpen source contributions: history of contributing to Rust, networking or distributed-systems open-source projects\nWhy Join Us?\nImpact at scale: Build the residential network tier behind web-scale data pipelines for top-tier global enterprises\nAutonomy and flexibility: Enjoy a genuine remote-first culture with flexible working hours and high organizational trust\nContinuous innovation: Solve emerging, complex technical challenges as AI and web data extraction rapidly evolve\nGlobal community: Collaborate with a passionate, diverse team of distributed systems engineers and data specialists across the world\nIf you are a Rust engineer who wants to turn tens of thousands of residential devices into dependable infrastructure, we would love to hear from you. Join us in building the fleet behind web data extraction at Zyte.\nBenefits\nBy joining the Zyte team, you will:\nBecome part of a self-motivated, progressive, multi-cultural team\nHave the freedom and flexibility to work from where you do your best work\nAttend conferences and meet with team members from across the globe\nWork with cutting-edge open source technologies and tools",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      }
    },
    "updated_at": "2026-11-03T23:29:51.290233+00:00"
  },
  "cache:posts": {
    "entries": {
      "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/alhazan-mubarak_fintech-nigeria-cloudcomputing-share-7516453508934422528-06Zm": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-03T23:31:43.023454+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "status": "active",
          "text": "I assumed AWS Local Zone in Lagos was the easy answer to the CBN localisation requirement. Then I sat down and read the documentation properly.\n\nIt isn't, at least not for the data layer.\n\nThere's no RDS in the Lagos Local Zone, so you'd be self-managing Postgres or MySQL on EC2. Also, Local Zones extend a parent Region (Lagos is linked to af-south-1), so EBS snapshots write to S3 in the parent Region by default. Local snapshots only work in Local Zones with S3 in-zone, and Lagos doesn't have that. So your backups end up in Cape Town.\n\nWhich leads to the bigger problem. There's no AWS Region in Nigeria. No Azure Region or Google Cloud Region either. If your payment database runs on a hyperscaler today, it's sitting in Ireland, Virginia or Cape Town — and so are your automated backups and your KMS keys.\n\nThe June circular requires payment transaction data generated in Nigeria to be stored and managed in Nigeria from 1 January 2027. That's under 90 days. For most teams, this isn't a settings change, because there's nowhere to point it at.\n\nThe harder question is what \"𝐬𝐭𝐨𝐫𝐞𝐝 𝐚𝐧𝐝 𝐦𝐚𝐧𝐚𝐠𝐞𝐝 𝐢𝐧 𝐍𝐢𝐠𝐞𝐫𝐢𝐚\" actually means in practice. Several law firms read it as covering the primary processing environment rather than just a copy held locally, which would mean backing up from a hyperscaler into Nigeria doesn't meet it. I put that question to Huawei Cloud directly and got the same answer, though they'd obviously have an interest in saying so.\n\nI've been working out how Nigerian startups can meet these requirements without needing a large infrastructure team or building everything from scratch.\n\nIf you're working through this at a Nigerian fintech or building infrastructure for one, I'd be glad to compare notes.\n\n#Fintech #Nigeria #CloudComputing #AWS",
          "posted_at": "2026-10-15T11:02:45.655Z"
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/betül-atiye-yalçın-56b2b4154_beytüşşebap-lokasyonumuzda-sorumluluk-almaya-share-7516098116530524160-C3k7": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-03T23:31:43.023454+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "status": "active",
          "text": "Beytüşşebap lokasyonumuzda sorumluluk almaya, sahada fark yaratmaya ve enerjisiyle değer katmaya hazır çalışma arkadaşlarımızı arıyoruz. ⚡",
          "posted_at": "2026-10-14T11:30:33.446Z"
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/china-produces-about-85-of-the-worlds-cathode-share-7516513337908633600-8_eD": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-03T23:31:43.023454+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "status": "active",
          "text": "China produces about 85% of the world's cathode active material. The West needs new battery chemistries to compete, but traditional R&D can take years to deliver them. \n \nToday, we announced $45M in funding to change that. \n \nBacked by  Zone II Ventures, and Course Corrected, we're scaling our AI-powered Discovery Engine, which combines 18 years of proprietary battery data with automated labs that physically build and test new materials. Over these 18 years our platform has run more than 225 projects for more than 85 customers across the battery value chain, including nearly a dozen Fortune 500 companies, and has resulted in more than 100 battery patents.  Along the way, the platform generated an internally consistent dataset covering more than 500,000 physical cells tested at over 165 million cycles.  \n \nOur technology has already helped deliver DRX, a new family of nickel- and cobalt-free cathode materials designed to reduce dependence on China. Now, we're bringing DRX toward commercialization while using AI to accelerate the next generation of breakthroughs. \n \nLed by founder and CEO Mathias Ingvarsson, COO and former Tesla manufacturing leader Steven Prast, and Chief Scientific Officer Dee Strand, we're building a faster path from battery discovery to commercial deployment. \n \nRead more in Fortune by Nick Lichtenberg. Article link in the first comment.",
          "posted_at": "2026-10-15T15:00:30.119Z"
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/heykristopher_xbox-is-building-a-new-kind-of-flywheel-with-ugcPost-7513955395246161920-7a3g": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-03T23:31:43.023454+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "status": "active",
          "text": "XBOX is building a new kind of flywheel with games at the center.\n\nThe company announced XP this morning (a clever title)—a new division headed by Kayleen Walters focused on creating more on-ramps for fans to its beloved IP through film & television, consumer products, live events, and strategic partnerships.\n\nHere are the four divisions:\n\n* XBOX PICTURES: Bringing our worlds and characters to new audiences through film, television, and other forms of linear storytelling. \n* XBOX PRODUCTS: Creating products that are authentic to the fandom that allow fans to celebrate and express the franchises they love. \n* XBOX PLACES: Bringing communities together through live events, immersive experiences, attractions, broadcasts, and destinations. \n* XBOX PARTNERSHIPS: Working with creators, brands, and communities to develop new experiences, sponsorships, and brand partnerships.\n\nThe move—championed by Matthew Ball following an internal memo from Asha Sharma—is both elegant and strategic. It adopts the best strategies from Disney and Nintendo, both of whom understand that content is king. Where Disney’s flywheel was built strategically around film and television firs, Nintendo’s is game first.\n\nWith this move, XBOX is positioning itself to move beyond being a mere platform to owning its market position as both a publisher and steward of massive IP (from Minecraft to Halo and beyond).\n\nI’m excited to see where this leads.",
          "posted_at": "2026-10-08T13:36:09.005Z"
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/moritzbaierlentz_game-studio-funding-is-back-gardens-interactive-share-7513608118791196673-sNWA": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-03T23:31:43.023454+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "status": "active",
          "text": "Game studio funding is back: Gardens Interactive has raised a $35M+ Series B, bringing total funding to over $70M before launching its flagship game.\n\nLed by Lightspeed, the round includes Sequoia Capital, Index Ventures, Accel, Eric Schmidt’s Innovation Endeavors, the Nintendo family (Yamauchi No.10), the ZeniMax Media family (James Altman), and the founders of Slack and OpenAI's Sora.\n\nBy any measure, but certainly in 2026, that's an extraordinary vote of confidence and tier-1 syndicate for a pre-launch studio. What inspires that conviction while it seems all venture dollars chase automation?\n\nA team creating a new genre around a simple and proven design principle: deepen human connections, and let the players be the fun.\n\nGardens calls it a “strandbox”: a social roleplaying world where chance encounters become adventures, players shape each other’s stories, and your actions leave something behind for whoever comes next.\n\nFrom serial game-of-the-year creators behind Journey and Sky, the team blends indie creativity and beautiful art with an ambitious AAA live-ops platform bet on how games can create significant and long-lasting emotional encounters.\n\nThis one is deeply personal. I love Stephen, 🔔Chris, and Lexie like brothers. After serving on Gardens’ board for the past three years, I’m rejoining as a personal investor and advisor, doubling down with my own capital and time. To continue an extraordinary development journey that already brought so many wonderful once-strangers together.\n\nI can’t wait for you all to play what they’re building.\n\nBloomberg exclusive by Cecilia D'Anastasio: https://lnkd.in/dYJ4Xj9C",
          "posted_at": "2026-10-07T14:36:12.326Z"
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/todd-simmons-55364412_north-carolina-at-students-march-back-to-activity-7516656598392483840-6xHl": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-03T23:31:43.023454+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "status": "active",
          "text": "Clarification: On Thursday, Oct. 15, thousands of Aggie students took part in TWO major marches to downtown Greensboro:\n\n- The first was a March to the Polls, as previously described, which went from campus to the Union Square polling location downtown on the first day of early voting in North Carolina. Students marched back to campus after voting in protest of the Guilford County Elections Board's removal of their campus early voting polling location earlier this year.\n\n- The second was a March for Justice for Nolan Wells, the 18-year-old young man who tragically died July 4 under murky circumstances in the waters off Mississippi’s Horn Island after celebrating the Independence Day holiday. The march was organized by the A&T chapter of the NAACP, and a coalition of groups worked tirelessly to bring students together in solidarity for Nolan from across campus and the entire state. The march began at A&T’s February One monument, went downtown to the International Civil Rights Museum and returned to campus.\n\nIncredibly, thousands of Aggies took part in *both* marches, but in the video posted here, were returning from the second march, which concluded later. In both instances, outstanding civic leadership and participation were on full display from A&T students in the best tradition of Aggies, who have been leading in important community events since the university’s establishment in 1891. \n\nA&T continues to be America's largest HBCU, as well as its top-rated public HBCU in Forbes and US News & World Report.",
          "posted_at": ""
        }
      }
    },
    "updated_at": "2026-11-03T23:31:43.023454+00:00"
  },
